<Base title="Privacy policy | WhichPadel" description="How WhichPadel collects and uses personal data."><article class="panel prose">
<h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="muted">Last updated: 20 October 2026. Draft: to be reviewed before launch.</p>
<p>This policy applies to https://whichpadel.com and explains how WhichPadel ("we") handles personal data under the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018. The data controller is [owner name and contact address, to be added before launch].</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2><ul>
<li><b>Email address</b> (and an optional maximum price), if you sign up for the newsletter or price drop alerts. Legal basis: your consent. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in every email.</li>
<li><b>Basic usage data</b> (pages viewed, approximate country, device type) if we add analytics. We will use privacy-friendly analytics where possible, and will ask for consent before setting any non-essential cookies, as required by PECR.</li>
<li><b>Affiliate clicks:</b> when you click a "Check price" link, the shop or affiliate network may set its own cookies to track the sale. Their privacy policies apply to that.</li></ul>
<h2>How we use it</h2><p>Only to send the emails you asked for, to understand which pages are useful, and to receive commission on sales. We do not sell your personal data.</p>
<h2>Who we share it with</h2><p>Our email provider and hosting provider (as processors), and affiliate networks for click tracking. Some may process data outside the UK under appropriate safeguards.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2><p>Email addresses: until you unsubscribe. Analytics: aggregated, kept no longer than needed.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2><p>You can ask to access, correct or delete your data, object to processing, or withdraw consent. Contact [contact email]. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</p>
</article></Base>
